cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper below."
title: PBP-ReID
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of "Efficient Body-Prior Token Anchoring and
  Part-Aware Global-Local Fusion for Multi-Scene Person Re-Identification":
  a ViT-Base person re-identification model with parameter-free body-prior token
  anchoring (EASA), hierarchical part-relation attention (HPRA) and
  global-local additive fusion (GAL).
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-09"
keywords:
  - person re-identification
  - part-aware representation
  - vision transformer
  - body prior
  - multi-scene robustness
  - inference efficiency
